# Accrue — deployment configuration
#
# Copy to .dev.vars for local development, or set each as a secret on the
# deployment. Never commit real values: .dev.vars and .env.local are ignored.
#
#   Cloudflare:  wrangler secret put ACCRUE_SPONSOR_KEY
#   Vercel:      vercel env add ACCRUE_SPONSOR_KEY production
#
# Every one of these is optional. Without it the app says what it cannot do
# rather than failing or pretending — so a deployment with none of them still
# runs, and still tells the truth about itself.

# Pays the first network fee for a new account, and claims its test AUSD.
# A private key for a funded Monad testnet account.
#
# Use a SEPARATE key from the contract deployer, funded with only what a demo
# needs — a few MON. Anyone holding this key can drain the account it belongs
# to, and reusing the deployer key means one leak costs both.
#
#   node scripts/deployer.mjs        prints an address to fund
#   https://faucet.monad.xyz         funds it
ACCRUE_SPONSOR_KEY=0x

# Payment history across the whole chain. The public RPC caps log queries at
# a hundred blocks, so without this the app can only show what it recorded
# itself, and it says so.
#   https://app.envio.dev/api-tokens
ENVIO_API_TOKEN=

# Range reads the public RPC refuses outright.
#   https://app.envio.dev/api-tokens
ENVIO_RPC_TOKEN=

# Cash-out to a bank account through Agora's routes. Also needs a verified
# bank account and an approved wallet entitlement on the Agora side, so this
# key alone is not enough to make redemption work.
#   https://app.agora.finance  →  API keys
#
# Agora's supply metrics need no key and always work.
AGORA_API_KEY=
